<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles-Godefroy de La Tour d'Auvergne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1706">1706</a>–<a href="/years/1771">1771</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles-Godefroy de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a> was a French nobleman, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederic-maurice-de-la-tour-dauvergne">Duke of Bouillon</a> from 1730 and the last viscount of Turenne. Burdened by his family's debts, in 1738 he sold the viscounty of Turenne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a>, ending its quasi-independent status and its tax privileges. Through his marriage to Maria Karolina Sobieska he was linked to the Polish royal family and the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-stuart">Stuarts</a>.</p></div>
